[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Leaf[/COLOR][COLOR=#2C3E50]RTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#7F8C8D]Free Random Teleport (RTP) Plugin for Paper, Spigot, Folia, Fabric, NeoForge & Velocity[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[CENTER][I]Once upon a time, I wanted to explore a minecraft world. I asked for [/I]/rtp[I] in servers I played on. They told me "no, that's laggy", and I took that personally.[/I][/CENTER]

[B]LeafRTP is a [/B][I]/rtp[/I][B] command.[/B] It teleports a player to a random, safe spot in the world, and works out those safe spots ahead of time (off the main server thread) so the teleport itself doesn't lag the server. Drop the jar in and [I]/rtp[/I] works with zero config, tune it in-game with [I]/rtp menu[/I], or build on the public [I]rtp-api[/I].

[B]At a glance:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Plug-and-play:[/B] drop the jar in, type [I]/rtp[/I], done. Zero config.
[*][B]No YAML required:[/B] tune regions, safety, and effects in-game with [I]/rtp menu[/I].
[*][B]One jar, every platform:[/B] build on the public [I]rtp-api[/I] and ship a single addon for all of them.
[*][B]No "Finding a safe location..." wait:[/B] destinations are pre-verified off-tick, never on the main thread.
[*][B]Measured on a public harness:[/B] 19.8 TP/s on Paper, 4 ms worst tick (next-best: 70 ms).
[*][B]Audited safety:[/B] no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim bypass, no silent failures.
[/LIST]

[CENTER]
[I]Minecraft 1.20.x / 1.21.x / 26.x. Legacy Forge isn't native; run this jar under Arclight / Mohist.[/I]

[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#16A085]Trusted since 2021: 4.6 stars over 30+ reviews, 430k+ downloads.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]Latest builds, Folia-tagged releases, and beta channels also live on [URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/leafrtp']Modrinth[/URL][/B] (auto-updater and Pterodactyl friendly).[/SIZE]

[/CENTER]
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]What makes it different[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Most [I]/rtp[/I] plugins pick a random point, load the chunk, and check if it's safe, retrying until one sticks. That's what stalls the server. Async alone doesn't fix it; it just moves the stall. What LeafRTP does differently is the low-latency, high-throughput engineering behind the two lookups every [I]/rtp[/I] depends on: where to send the player, and whether that spot is safe. Those are four named mechanisms.

[SIZE=4][B]Archimedean spiral[/B][/SIZE]
Destinations come off a space-filling Archimedean spiral curve, a single indexed mapping from one number to a coordinate. Every reachable spot has equal odds instead of piling players near spawn, and picking one is a lookup rather than a reroll. The math, with distribution plots: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/site/why/'][I]Why LeafRTP exists[/I][/URL].

[SIZE=4][B]Spatial memory[/B][/SIZE]
A persistent spatial memory records which sectors already failed safety checks, so the selector skips known-bad ground instead of rerolling forever. Search time stays predictable as a region fills up.

[SIZE=4][B]Anvil pre-filter[/B][/SIZE]
An Anvil ([I].mca[/I]) pre-filter reads biome and block data straight from the region files on disk, so unsafe spots are rejected before a chunk is ever loaded. That is the biome lookup done in bulk and off the tick loop, which is where most of the throughput comes from. It also reads what the world actually contains, not what the generator predicts: the common shortcuts ([I]getBiome[/I], [I]getHighestBlockAt[/I]) answer from the generation noise map, which can disagree with the real terrain once a spot has been edited or carried across a Minecraft version. Checking the saved data means the safety verdict matches the world the player lands in. How the engine stays off-tick: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/FOR_CONTRIBUTORS/'][I]Architecture[/I][/URL].

[SIZE=4][B]Pre-verified cache[/B][/SIZE]
Because selection is cheap and the pre-filter is fast, safe destinations are kept ready in a cache, so serving [I]/rtp[/I] is mostly handing back a coordinate that's already checked. The numbers are in the benchmark section below.

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Zero-config install:[/B] drop the jar in, type [I]/rtp[/I], done. A [I]default[/I] region is ready on first boot.
[*][B]In-game tuning:[/B] [I]/rtp menu[/I] browses worlds and regions and changes settings live. No YAML, no restart.
[*][B]12 claim integrations bundled[/B] (GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, WorldGuard, Towny, Lands, +7 more). No teleport into protected land.
[*][B]Vault economy:[/B] optional charge per teleport, per-region pricing, auto-refund on cancel.
[*][B]Effects engine:[/B] particles, sounds, fireworks, potions on every teleport phase.
[*][B]Per-player cooldowns & usage limits[/B] out of the box.
[*][B]PvP/combat-tag gate, PlaceholderAPI, live map heatmaps, multi-world overrides.[/B]
[*][B]Folia, out of the box:[/B] regionized scheduling + async teleport, no paid tier.
[*][B]Cross-server [I]/rtp[/I] without Redis or SQL:[/B] the [I]proxy-direct[/I] Velocity transport ships in the free build.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Build on it[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
The whole plugin runs on the public [I]rtp-api[/I], the same surface you get. Every feature above is wired through it, so you extend LeafRTP instead of forking it, and one addon jar runs unchanged on Spigot, Paper, Folia, Fabric, and NeoForge. The [I]rtp-api[/I] hooks take one-line suppliers to veto destinations, charge economy, add placeholders, override the world border, gate combat, replace the bare [I]/rtp[/I] action, register a new region shape, or build custom arrival platforms. The bundled GUI addon does exactly this, swapping bare [I]/rtp[/I] for its own picker. Full API guide: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/FOR_ADDON_DEVELOPERS/']addon / API developer guide[/URL].

[CENTER][IMG]https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TZNIQSHX/images/c80c085c001f5fbc1c2a14ae01c10e0540c26fc9.webp[/IMG]
[I]A real [I]/rtp[/I] landing: pre-verified destination served in [B]0 attempts, 49 ms[/B] (1 gametick) on Folia, no "Finding a safe location..." wait. The title, sound, and effects shown are fully configurable.[/I][/CENTER]

Performance is in the numbers, not the prose: on Paper, LeafRTP holds a 4 ms worst tick where the next-best plugin hits 70 ms. Full Paper/Spigot/Folia tables and methodology are in the benchmark section below; reproduce them on your own rig: [URL=https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP][I]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/I][/URL]. (How each feature stays cheap: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/FOR_CONTRIBUTORS/'][I]Architecture[/I][/URL].)

[SPOILER='Verification & sources']
Every number on this page is anchored in the repo:
[LIST]
[*][B]Reproducible benchmarks[/B] with raw CSVs and per-run analyses: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP'][B]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]Requirements traced to tests:[/B] every requirement, including the safety prohibitions, has an implementing class and regression test: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/TRACEABILITY.md'][B]TRACEABILITY.md[/B][/URL]
[*][B]Every design decision is documented:[/B] dated, linkable notes on why teleports are queued, how the Anvil pre-filter skips chunk loads, and more: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/docs/adr'][B]docs/adr/[/B][/URL]
[*][B]bStats[/B] enabled. Anonymous usage stats help prioritize platform work.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Watch it work[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[I]/rtp scan[/I] paints region safety onto a real in-game map (green safe, red unsafe) [B]as it verifies it[/B], off-tick on every platform. [I]/rtp info[/I] reports live TPS/MSPT, heap, latency percentiles, and rejection causes, no metrics add-on needed.

[URL='https://youtu.be/Ftjy1zw_S04'][B]Watch the scan paint a region live (video)[/B][/URL]. Details: [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/COMMANDS/'][B]Scan & spatial memory[/B][/URL], [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/admin/RUNBOOK/'][B]Diagnostics[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#C0392B]Requirements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Hard requirements. If any are a [B]no[/B], EssentialsX [I]/rtp[/I] or HuskHomes are fine alternatives.

[LIST]
[*][B]Java 21+[/B] (REQ-RTP-SYS-001, non-negotiable).
[*][B]Paper, Spigot, or a Bukkit-family fork[/B], or Fabric / NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x). Arclight / Mohist for Forge bridges.
[*][B]Vault[/B] (optional) for the economy charge; dormant when not installed.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#16A085]Install (30 seconds)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [I]LeafRTP-x.y.z.jar[/I] into [I]plugins/[/I].
[*]Start the server. A [I]default[/I] region is generated for you.
[*]Type [B]/rtp[/B].
[*]Run [B]/rtp menu[/B] to browse regions, worlds, and configuration in-game (clickable book on Paper / Folia, chat-paginated fallback elsewhere).
[/LIST]

Tune [I]plugins/RTP/config.yml[/I] and [I]plugins/RTP/regions/*.yml[/I] later, via [I]/rtp menu[/I] or by editing the YAML directly. Full admin guide is auto-unpacked into [I]plugins/RTP/docs/[/I] on first run, and lives online at the [URL='https://dailystruggle.github.io/RTP/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS/'][B]admin guide[/B][/URL].

[B]Bundled addons unpack themselves on first run.[/B] Four addon jars ride inside the LeafRTP jar and self-extract into [I]plugins/RTP/addons/[/I] the first time the plugin starts - no second download. Delete one from that folder to turn it off (the folder then exists, so it is never re-extracted):
[LIST]
[*][B]LeafRTPGuiAddon[/B] (GUI demo) - a clickable chest destination-picker. It binds the bare [I]/rtp[/I] root action, so with a GUI renderer present typing [I]/rtp[/I] opens the picker instead of teleporting immediately (instant teleport stays reachable from the menu and as a fallback), and adds [I]/rtp gui[/I] ([I]rtp.gui[/I]).
[*][B]LeafRTPClaimAddon[/B] (claim integrations) - the 12 claim/protection checkers, so claim-aware teleport works out of the box on the Bukkit family.
[*][B]LeafRTPRiftAddon[/B] (effect demo) - registers a "Virtual Rift" teleport effect that tears the terrain open into a void during warmup (presentation-only client-side blocks, so it can never compromise safety), usable by name in [I]effects/*.yml[/I].
[*][B]LeafRTPCountdownAddon[/B] (addon-system reference demo) - live teleport and queue-position countdowns, and the canonical copy-paste reference addon.
[/LIST]

For those interested in writing their own: every one of these is shipped as a worked coding example. Their full source lives under [I]addons/[/I] in the repo, and the Rift and Countdown demos are pure [I]rtp-api[/I] / [I]effects-api[/I] (zero platform imports), so they double as copy-paste starting points for your own addon.

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SPOILER='Full free feature list (click to expand)']
[LIST]
[*][B]Deterministic spiral selection:[/B] bounded math, no unbounded re-roll loops. Predictable on huge worlds.
[*][B]Spatial memory that persists across restarts:[/B] LeafRTP [I]learns[/I] which sectors keep failing and stops trying them.
[*]Most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve instantly from a [B]pre-generated location queue[/B]: destinations are chunk-loaded and verified before you type the command.
[*][B]Safety pipeline:[/B] radius check, invulnerability timer, optional landing platform, movement / damage cancel timers, material allow/deny list.
[*][B]Optional PvP / combat-tag gate:[/B] off by default; when enabled, /rtp is refused or delayed for players who recently dealt or took PvP damage, so a teleport can't be used to escape a fight. Native combat tracking, with optional PvPManager / CombatLogX / Simple Combat Log integration.
[*][B]Per-region arrival schematics:[/B] drop a [I].schem[/I] named after a region into [I]plugins/RTP/schematics/[/I] and every teleport into that region pastes it (a lobby pad, arrival shrine, or custom platform) on the landing spot. Cross-platform Sponge [I].schem[/I], decoded in-house (no WorldEdit required), claim-aware and audited.
[*][B]Per-region, per-world config:[/B] shapes (square / circle / rectangle), curve weighting, vertical adjustors, sky-light check, world overrides, hot-reloadable YAML.
[*][B]Effects on every lifecycle phase:[/B] particles, sounds, fireworks, potion, note effects via the in-tree [I]effects-api[/I], gated by [I]rtp.effects.<name>[/I] permissions.
[*][B]Twelve claim-plugin integrations bundled:[/B] GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, TownyAdvanced, SaberFactions, FactionsBridge, HuskClaims, RedProtect, CrashClaim, KingdomsX, Residence.
[*]Iris, Terra, and custom datapack generators work out of the box, with modded biome IDs preserved. [B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] and [B]ProtocolLib[/B] are supported as optional soft-deps.
[*][B]Optional Vault economy:[/B] charge players per [I]/rtp[/I] with per-region price, [I]priceOther[/I], params/biome surcharges, and a balance floor ([I]economy.yml[/I]); cost refunded automatically on cancel or pipeline failure ([I]refundOnCancel: true[/I] default); dormant when Vault is not installed.
[*][B]Public [I]rtp-api[/I][/B]: same surface as Pro. Trigger LeafRTP from a GUI, NPC, or quest; build your own UX without forking.
[*][B]Platform-agnostic addons:[/B] addons compile against [I]rtp-api[/I] only and load through the [I]RTPAddon[/I] ServiceLoader SPI, so one addon module runs unchanged on Spigot, Paper, Folia, Fabric, and NeoForge. Config, safety hooks, teleport-pipeline callbacks, and scheduling are reached through platform-neutral APIs; you only add a platform module when the addon opens a platform-native UI. Four demo addons (GUI, claim, effect, reference) self-extract into [I]plugins/RTP/addons/[/I] on first run - see the bundled LeafRTPRiftAddon and LeafRTPCountdownAddon demos.
[*][B]Live map / heatmap visualizations:[/B] [I]/rtp scan[/I] paints region safety state (green safe / red unsafe) onto a real held map item while the chat readout streams cps, land %, and ETA. Free on Paper, Spigot, Fabric, and NeoForge.
[*][B]Built-in runtime observability:[/B] [I]/rtp info[/I] reports TPS/MSPT (spark-enhanced when spark is installed), JVM heap, pipeline latency percentiles, generation success/failure breakdown, and a [I]/rtp info biomes[/I] player-occupancy leaderboard, no metrics add-on needed.
[*][B]12 locales, parity-enforced:[/B] shipped locales are CI-verified so a translated server never silently falls back to English on a new key.
[*][B]Every feature's design is documented:[/B] the reasoning behind each capability and a requirements-to-tests trace, all public: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/INDEX.md'][B]docs/dev/INDEX.md[/B][/URL].
[/LIST]

